            <ArticleTitle>Two-year outcomes after enhanced external counterpulsation for stable angina pectoris (from the International EECP Patient Registry [IEPR]).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>461-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We assessed the long-term outcomes of enhanced external counterpulsation in relieving angina and improving the quality of life in a large cohort of patients with chronic angina pectoris. Seventy-three percent had a reduction by &gt; or =1 angina class at the end of treatment, and 50% reported an improvement in the quality-of-life assessment after enhanced external counterpulsation; these results were sustained at 2-year follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
